---
description: Enforces the tool transformation model and make command usage for consistent development workflows
globs: **/*
alwaysApply: true
---

# tool-transformation-enforcement.mdc

meta:
  name: Tool Transformation Enforcement
  description: >
    Enforces the tool transformation model and make command usage for consistent development
    workflows. Ensures all tools are used as transformation agents with proper input/output
    relationships and integrated workflows through Makefile orchestration.

rules:
  - when: tool.execution
    then:
      - "All tools are transformation agents converting input to output"
      - "Use make targets for development workflow orchestration"
      - "Prefer uv over pip for Python package management"
      - "Map PDCA phases to appropriate make targets"
      - "Validate transformations with appropriate tools"

  - when: development.workflow
    then:
      - "Use make run for application execution"
      - "Use make run-dev for development mode"
      - "Use make setup-dev for environment setup"
      - "Use make check for comprehensive validation"
      - "Use make commands for all operations"

  - when: test.workflow
    then:
      - "Use make test for test execution"
      - "Use make test-cov for test coverage"
      - "Use make test-fast for fast tests only"
      - "Use make test-integration for integration tests"
      - "Use make test-unit for unit tests"
      - "Never use direct pytest calls"

  - when: build.workflow
    then:
      - "Use make build for package building"
      - "Use make clean for cleaning artifacts"
      - "Use make install for runtime dependencies"
      - "Use make install-dev for development dependencies"
      - "Use uv build for modern Python builds"

  - when: code.quality
    then:
      - "Use make lint for all linting checks"
      - "Use make format for code formatting"
      - "Use make pre-commit for pre-commit hooks"
      - "Use black for code formatting"
      - "Use ruff for fast linting"
      - "Use flake8 for style enforcement"

  - when: documentation.workflow
    then:
      - "Use make docs for documentation building"
      - "Use make docs-serve for local documentation"
      - "Use mkdocs for documentation site generation"
      - "Use markdown processors for content transformation"

  - when: dependency.management
    then:
      - "Use uv pip install for package installation"
      - "Use uv pip install -r requirements-dev.txt for dev dependencies"
      - "Use uv build for package building"
      - "Use uv sync for dependency synchronization"
      - "Never use direct pip commands"

  - when: pdca.workflow
    then:
      - "PLAN: make test, make lint"
      - "DO: make docs, read relevant files"
      - "CHECK: make test-cov, make lint"
      - "ACT: make format, make build, make test"

  - when: artifact.processing
    then:
      - "Use PyYAML/ruamel.yaml for MDC processing"
      - "Use rdflib for TTL/RDF processing"
      - "Use markdown processors for markdown transformation"
      - "Use pip-tools for requirements management"
      - "Use structured libraries for all file operations"

  - when: forbidden.tools
    then:
      - "Do not use direct pytest calls (use make test)"
      - "Do not use direct pip install (use uv)"
      - "Do not use manual file operations (use structured tools)"
      - "Do not bypass make command orchestration"
      - "Do not use unstructured tool calls"

transformation_model:
  build_tools:
    make:
      input: "Makefile, source files"
      output: "Built artifacts, test results"
      command: "make [target]"
      description: "Build and development workflow orchestration"

    uv:
      input: "pyproject.toml, requirements files"
      output: "Installed packages, built distributions"
      command: "uv [command]"
      description: "Python package and dependency management"

    hatchling:
      input: "pyproject.toml, source files"
      output: "Built packages"
      command: "hatchling build"
      description: "Python package building"

  testing_tools:
    pytest:
      input: "Test files, source files"
      output: "Test results, coverage data"
      command: "make test"
      description: "Test execution and PDCA phase tracking"

    coverage:
      input: "Test execution data"
      output: "Coverage reports"
      command: "make test-cov"
      description: "Test coverage measurement"

    mypy:
      input: "Python source files"
      output: "Type checking results"
      command: "make lint"
      description: "Type checking and model validation"

  code_quality:
    black:
      input: "Python source files"
      output: "Formatted source files"
      command: "make format"
      description: "Code formatting"

    ruff:
      input: "Python source files"
      output: "Linting results"
      command: "make lint"
      description: "Fast Python linting"

    flake8:
      input: "Python source files"
      output: "Style check results"
      command: "make lint"
      description: "Style guide enforcement"

  documentation:
    mkdocs:
      input: "Markdown files, configuration"
      output: "Documentation site"
      command: "make docs"
      description: "Documentation site generation"

    markdown_processors:
      input: "Markdown content"
      output: "Processed markdown"
      command: "markdown-it-py, mistune, panflute"
      description: "Markdown content transformation"

  artifact_processors:
    mdc:
      input: "MDC files with YAML frontmatter"
      output: "Structured MDC data"
      command: "PyYAML, ruamel.yaml"
      description: "Model Definition Card processing"

    ttl:
      input: "Turtle/RDF files"
      output: "RDF graph data"
      command: "rdflib"
      description: "Turtle/RDF processing"

    requirements:
      input: "Requirements files"
      output: "Resolved dependencies"
      command: "pip-tools"
      description: "Requirements file management"

enforcement:
  required_commands:
    - "make test - Test execution"
    - "make test-cov - Test coverage"
    - "make lint - Code quality checks"
    - "make format - Code formatting"
    - "make build - Package building"
    - "make clean - Clean artifacts"
    - "uv pip install - Package installation"
    - "uv build - Modern Python builds"

  forbidden_commands:
    - "pytest [direct calls]"
    - "pip install [direct calls]"
    - "python -m pytest"
    - "Manual file operations"
    - "Unstructured tool calls"

  validation:
    - "All tool calls must use make commands"
    - "Package management must use uv"
    - "File operations must use structured libraries"
    - "PDCA phases must map to make targets"
    - "Transformations must have clear input/output"

examples:
  correct_workflow:
    scenario: "Running tests and validation"
    commands:
      - "make test - Run test suite"
      - "make test-cov - Run tests with coverage"
      - "make lint - Check code quality"
      - "make format - Format code"
      - "make build - Build package"

  incorrect_workflow:
    scenario: "Direct tool calls (forbidden)"
    commands:
      - "pytest tests/ - Direct pytest call"
      - "pip install package - Direct pip call"
      - "python -m pytest - Direct pytest call"
      - "Manual file editing - Unstructured operations"

  pdca_tool_mapping:
    scenario: "PDCA workflow with tools"
    plan:
      - "make test - Identify failing tests"
      - "make lint - Identify code quality issues"
    do:
      - "make docs - Generate current documentation"
      - "Read relevant source files"
    check:
      - "make test-cov - Validate with coverage"
      - "make lint - Verify code quality"
    act:
      - "make format - Format code changes"
      - "make build - Build updated package"
      - "make test - Validate all changes"

  transformation_example:
    scenario: "Processing MDC files"
    input: "MDC file with YAML frontmatter and markdown content"
    transformation: "PyYAML for YAML parsing + markdown processor for content"
    output: "Structured MDC data with validated content"
    command: "Structured library calls"

rationale: >
  Tool transformation enforcement ensures:
  - Consistent tool usage across the project
  - Clear mapping of tools to their transformation purpose
  - Integration of PDCA workflow with build tools
  - Standardized development workflow through Makefile
  - Modern Python development practices with UV
  - Proper artifact processing for all file types
  - Systematic approach to tool selection and usage

  This enforcement prevents:
  - Inconsistent tool usage
  - Manual workflow steps
  - Tool conflicts and version issues
  - Lack of integration between tools
  - Inefficient development workflows
  - Direct tool calls bypassing orchestration
  - Unstructured file operations

  Recent violations that this rule addresses:
  - Direct pytest calls instead of make test
  - Direct pip install instead of uv
  - Manual file operations without structured libraries
  - Bypassing make command orchestration
  - Inconsistent tool usage patterns

---

This rule ensures all tools are properly used as transformation agents with clear input/output relationships and integrated workflows through Makefile orchestration.
description:
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---
